{"parentUuid":"941fe160-a521-4b27-b4ba-821c54f70ad3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNJMJGXd2NUjDDjigpmt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N47gkn5CcYPBYKBtsuqWRb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize; git add internal/cli/history.go internal/cli/history_oversize_tolerance_test.go && git status --short | head; git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nMerge origin/main into fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize\n\nmain's COR-2268 refactor moved the overridable read bounds and the size-refusal\nerror into internal/cli/internal/base and exported their names, touching the\nexact lines this branch rewrites.\n\nResolved toward this branch's structure — the sentinel plus\nhistoryTranscriptTooLargeError, which is the point of the change — while\nadopting main's names: base.MaxDocumentTranscriptBytes at all four sites\n(the bare constant no longer exists) and base.ReadBoundExceededError's\nexported fields in the store-path test.\n\nRe-proved after merging rather than assumed: the three guards run and pass,\nmain's TestOverridableProductionBoundsKeepTheirDefaults still passes (so the\ntest's bound override does not leak), and weakening the identity reader's skip\nturns both index guards red.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the merge resolution"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":393,"cache_read_input_tokens":153336,"output_tokens":603,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":118},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":393,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":603,"cache_read_input_tokens":153336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":393,"cache_creation":{"ep